  "id": "DrugBank_DB00808 - MONDO_5044",
  "verbalization": "Indapamide is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hypertensive Disorder through a series of indirect but interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Indapamide is associated with Hypertension, which in turn is linked to Xipamide, a compound that is also associated with Hypertensive Disorder. This indicates a potential role of Indapamide in the development of hypertension, which may then contribute to the manifestation of Hypertensive Disorder. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Indapamide to Hypertensive Disorder highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Indapamide potentially acting as a mediator in the transition from hypertension to the disorder. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering Indapamide's role in the broader context of hypertension management and its potential reutilization in treating Hypertensive Disorder.",
